From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:21:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: macaudio: give each card its own jack pins

snd_soc_jack_add_pins() links the pins it is given into the jack's pin
list through their own list heads. macaudio passes every card the same
static array. That works with one card per machine, but the J616s
headphone jack becomes a card of its own next to the speaker card.

With two cards, the second card to probe re-links the shared pins into
its own jack. The first card's pin list then runs into the second card's
list head, and its next jack report dereferences garbage as a pin name.
On the J616s that oopsed the CS42L84 interrupt thread at boot and left
jack detection dead until the next boot.

Copy the pins into the card's own data and keep the template const.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 6156ff623f29781906a7532b85801dc4539f75a9)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index f860039d76..c3a646d6d4 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -148,6 +148,8 @@ struct ma_codec_idle {
 struct macaudio_snd_data {
 	struct snd_soc_card card;
 	struct snd_soc_jack jack;
+	/* The jack links these into its pin list, so each card needs its own */
+	struct snd_soc_jack_pin jack_pins[2];
 	int jack_plugin_state;
 
 	const struct macaudio_platform_cfg *cfg;
@@ -1391,7 +1393,7 @@ static int macaudio_fe_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 					(1 << nslots) - 1, nslots, MACAUDIO_SLOTWIDTH);
 }
 
-static struct snd_soc_jack_pin macaudio_jack_pins[] = {
+static const struct snd_soc_jack_pin macaudio_jack_pins[] = {
 	{
 		.pin = "Headphone",
 		.mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
@@ -1409,12 +1411,15 @@ static int macaudio_probe(struct snd_soc_card *card)
 
 	dev_dbg(card->dev, "%s!\n", __func__);
 
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(ma->jack_pins) != sizeof(macaudio_jack_pins));
+	memcpy(ma->jack_pins, macaudio_jack_pins, sizeof(ma->jack_pins));
+
 	ret = snd_soc_card_jack_new_pins(card, "Headphone Jack",
 			SND_JACK_HEADSET | SND_JACK_HEADPHONE |
 			SND_JACK_BTN_0 | SND_JACK_BTN_1 |
 			SND_JACK_BTN_2 | SND_JACK_BTN_3,
-			&ma->jack, macaudio_jack_pins,
-			ARRAY_SIZE(macaudio_jack_pins));
+			&ma->jack, ma->jack_pins,
+			ARRAY_SIZE(ma->jack_pins));
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(card->dev, "jack creation failed: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
